# Email settings for running ArxivDaily on your own computer.
#
# 1. Copy this file to ".env" (same folder as main.py). ".env" is git-ignored,
#    so your password never ends up in the repository.
# 2. Fill in the two required lines below.
# 3. Run:  python main.py --check        (logs in, sends nothing)
#          python main.py --test-email   (sends one test email)
#
# On GitHub you don't need this file: add the same names as repository secrets
# (Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions).

# Required: your full email address and an app password (not your login password).
SMTP_USERNAME=you@gmail.com
SMTP_PASSWORD=abcd efgh ijkl mnop

# Optional: who receives the digest (comma-separated). Default: SMTP_USERNAME.
# MAIL_TO=you@gmail.com, colleague@university.edu

# Optional: only needed if your provider isn't detected automatically
# (Gmail, iCloud, Yahoo, QQ, 163, 126, Zoho, Fastmail, GMX, AOL and Yandex are).
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_SECURITY=starttls
# SMTP_FROM=you@example.com
